@node Fountain Frontend
@section Fountain Frontend

The Fountain frontend is a language front-end for the EIGHTBOL compiler that 
emits canonical AST nodes per the frontend_conformance.texi specification.

Fountain is a screenwriting and interactive fiction language designed for 
game scripting and narrative development.

@subsection Canonical AST Node Implementation

The Fountain frontend fully implements the canonical AST specification:

@itemize
@item @code{:move} — Assignment (SET, MOVE operations)
@item @code{:add}, @code{:subtract}, @code{:multiply}, @code{:divide} — Arithmetic 
  operations (SUM OF, DIFFERENCE OF, PRODUCT OF, QUOTIENT OF)
@item @code{:shift-left}, @code{:shift-right} — Bit shift operations (SHIFT LEFT OF, SHIFT RIGHT OF)
@item @code{:if} — Conditional statements (WHEN, UNLESS, IF/ELSE)
@item @code{:perform} — Loops (REPEAT n TIMES, BEGIN/UNTIL, BEGIN/WHILE/REPEAT)
@item @code{:evaluate} — Multi-way dispatch (COND with WHEN/WHEN-OTHER clauses)
@item @code{:procedure} — Procedure definitions (scripts)
@item @code{:goto} — Label jumps (# labels)
@item @code{:inspect} — String inspection (LENGTH OF, CHARACTER AT, POSITION OF, COUNT OF)
@item @code{:subscript} — Array access (FROM array ELEMENT index)
@item @code{:refmod} — Reference modification/substring (SUBSTRING OF...FROM...TO)
@item @code{:address-of} — Address-of operation (ADDRESS OF var)
@item @code{:string-blt} — Block copy (BLOCK COPY OF source TO dest)
@item @code{:null} — Null value literal and tests (NULL, Is Null, Is Not Null)
@item @code{:self} — Self reference (Self)
@end itemize

@subsection Arithmetic Word Syntax

Fountain uses English-like syntax for arithmetic operations, all emitting
canonical binary expression nodes:

@example
SUM OF e1, e2           → (:add :from e1 :to e2 :giving nil)
DIFFERENCE OF e1, e2    → (:subtract :minuend e1 :subtrahend e2 :giving nil)
PRODUCT OF e1, e2       → (:multiply :multiplicand e1 :multiplier e2 :giving nil)
QUOTIENT OF e1, e2      → (:divide :numerator e1 :denominator e2 :giving nil)
@end example

Infix operators also produce canonical nodes:

@example
e1 + e2  → :add
e1 - e2  → :subtract
e1 * e2  → :multiply
e1 / e2  → :divide
@end example

@subsection Shift Operations

Bit shift operations use English word syntax:

@example
SHIFT LEFT OF expr      → (:shift-left expr count)
SHIFT RIGHT OF expr     → (:shift-right expr count)
@end example

@subsection Control Flow Statements

@code{WHEN} and @code{UNLESS} conditionals emit @code{:if} nodes:

@example
WHEN condition THEN ... → (:if :condition condition :then stmts :else nil)
UNLESS condition THEN ..→ (:if :condition (:not condition) :then stmts :else nil)
@end example

@code{REPEAT n TIMES} emits @code{:perform}:

@example
REPEAT 10 TIMES ... → (:perform :procedure nil :times 10 :body stmts)
@end example

@code{COND} statements emit @code{:evaluate}:

@example
COND WHEN c1 ... ELSE WHEN c2 ... ELSE ... 
  → (:evaluate :clauses ((:when :condition c1 :statements ...)
                          (:when :condition c2 :statements ...)
                          (:when-other :statements ...)))
@end example

@subsection Null and Self References

The Fountain frontend supports null value and self-reference literals:

@example
NULL                 → :null
SELF                 → :self
NULLIFY $var         → (:move :from :null :to var)
var Is Null          → (:null var)
var Is Not Null      → (:not-null var)
@end example

@subsection String Inspection

String inspection functions emit @code{:inspect} nodes with appropriate
operation keywords:

@example
LENGTH OF string             → (:inspect :length string)
CHARACTER AT n OF string     → (:inspect :character string n)
POSITION OF substring IN str → (:inspect :position str substring)
COUNT OF substring IN str    → (:inspect :count str substring)
@end example

@subsection Array Access

Array subscripting uses FROM...ELEMENT syntax:

@example
FROM $arr ELEMENT $index → (:subscript arr index)
@end example

@subsection String Operations

Reference modification and string operations:

@example
SUBSTRING OF str FROM start TO end  → (:refmod :base str :start start :length end)
ADDRESS OF var                      → (:address-of var)
BLOCK COPY OF src TO dest           → (:string-blt :source src :dest dest)
@end example

@subsection Lexer Features

The Fountain lexer tokenizes source code and normalizes identifiers to PascalCase.
All keywords are case-insensitive and recognized by token type.

Supported number formats:
@itemize
@item Decimal numbers (123, 0)
@item Hexadecimal (0xFF)
@item Binary (0b1010)
@item Octal (0o77)
@end itemize

@subsection Module Structure

The Fountain frontend is organized into:

@itemize
@item @code{package.lisp} — Package definition
@item @code{lexer.lisp} — Tokenization and keyword recognition
@item @code{parser.lisp} — AST node generation with canonical node emission
@item @code{tests.lisp} — Conformance tests
@end itemize

@subsection Implementation Notes

- All arithmetic words produce canonical binary operator nodes, not non-standard nodes
- SET operations unconditionally emit @code{:move} nodes
- Control flow structures emit canonical @code{:if} and @code{:perform} nodes
- String inspection always emits @code{:inspect} nodes with appropriate operation keywords
- All backends receive canonical AST only; no backend-specific transformations are needed
